WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
A web interface can make the assistant accessible across approved devices,

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.440
while a desktop interface may simplify one-user local operation.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.350
Choose according to authentication, network exposure, file handling, support,

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.310
and accessibility needs.

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.875
Chat history helps continuity but increases privacy and context risk.

00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:19.445
Let users understand what is retained, where it is stored,

00:00:19.445 --> 00:00:21.590
and how to delete or start a clean session.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:24.800
Do not silently place unlimited history into every request.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.075
System instructions define role, boundaries, format, source use, and escalation.

00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:31.321
Prompt templates support repeatable workflows.

00:00:31.321 --> 00:00:32.860
Neither is a security boundary;

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.920
users and retrieved content can still influence model behavior.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.090
Document upload needs file-size, type, malware, privacy, storage, retention,

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.030
and authorization controls.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.520
Search should show useful source context.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.520
Speech and voice features add microphones, audio files, transcription, synthesis,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.390
and possibly third-party services.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:54.085
Usability includes time to first token, response speed, progress feedback, cancellation,

00:00:54.085 --> 00:00:57.971
errors, citations, copy or export, and recovery after restart.

00:00:57.971 --> 00:01:02.269
A slow assistant with unclear status feels unreliable even when answers are strong.

00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:03.470
Design for correction.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.825
Users should flag unsupported answers, inspect sources, retry safely,

00:01:06.825 --> 00:01:08.655
and know when to contact a human.

00:01:08.655 --> 00:01:12.362
The interface should make uncertainty and boundaries visible without burying the workflow

00:01:12.362 --> 00:01:13.880
in warnings.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.520
Accessibility is part of usability.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.720
Keyboard navigation, readable contrast, clear focus, captions or transcripts for audio,

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:20.765
understandable errors,

00:01:20.765 --> 00:01:24.750
and screen-reader-friendly structure determine whether authorized users can operate the

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.840
assistant reliably.
